Match the pairing code in your AI host. Windows reports the bridge's parent process. Use the pairing code to confirm which host connection receives access. Programs and chats that share this connection can use this permission.

The host can read the current screen and search retained terminal history, including the normal screen behind a full-screen application. Text from before sharing or while sharing was off is included if still retained. The bridge runs locally. The host may keep this data or send it to an external model, depending on its settings.

Use End AI sharing to stop future reads. Sharing again gives the recipient access to the history still retained then.

