Match the pairing code in your AI host. Windows reports the bridge's parent process. Use the pairing code to confirm which host connection receives access. Programs and chats that share this connection can use this permission.

The host can send keys and multiple lines of commands without asking again, with all permissions available in the connected terminal. Taking control back stops new AI input and keeps output shared. Choose End AI sharing before entering a password or one-time code.
